# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RUN OUTPUTS — ALL OF THEM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Even in a private repository this is worth keeping deliberate. A run output is
# the most sensitive thing here and the least reviewed: nobody reads a 40 MB
# device log before committing it, and git keeps it forever in every clone.
#
# Commit a run when it is EVIDENCE someone will come back to — the record behind
# a published number, a reproduction of a bug. Force that to be a decision by
# excluding the class and adding the exception, rather than the reverse.
#
# Blanket, and with no negations: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so "results/" plus "!results/README.md" silently drops
# the README. Layout docs belong beside the workflow instead.
results/
**/results/

# Oversized raw logs, if you keep any results at all. A device that is entirely
# off the network repeats one failure with a full stack trace for the whole
# window — tens of MB with a few thousand unique lines. Commit the sibling
# <id>.md summary; leave the raw file local.
# projects/<project>/results/<run>/logs/<id>.log
